---
import Base from '~/layouts/Base.astro';
import Frame from '~/components/Frame.astro';
import Tag from '~/components/Tag.astro';
import '~/styles/prose.css';
---

<Base title="Privacy" description="What this site measures, and what it doesn't.">
  <article class="privacy">
    <Frame corners="tri">
      <Tag label="Privacy" />
      <h1>No cookies.</h1>
      <p class="sub">What this site measures, and what it doesn't.</p>
    </Frame>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        This site uses <a href="https://umami.is">Umami</a> for privacy-first analytics. It sets no
        cookies, stores nothing on your device, collects no personal data, and doesn't track you
        across other sites. If your browser sends Do Not Track, nothing is recorded.
      </p>
      <h2>What is counted</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Page views, time on site, referrer, country, browser, OS and device type.</li>
        <li>
          Which terminal commands are run: the command name only (<code>help</code>,<code>ls</code>
          ), never what you type after it.
        </li>
        <li>Clicks on project links, contact links, and the résumé page.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        That's everything. The data is aggregated in Umami and used only to see what's useful on
        this site. Questions: <a href="mailto:trevorst18@gmail.com">trevorst18@gmail.com</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .privacy {
    display: grid;
    gap: 36px;
    padding-top: 48px;
  }
</style>
